# Day 34 – Dockerizing a Node.js Application

## 📚 What I Learned

Today I learned how to containerize a simple Node.js application using Docker.

## Topics Covered
- What is a Dockerfile?
- Difference between Docker Image and Docker Container
- Understanding Dockerfile instructions:
  - FROM
  - WORKDIR
  - COPY
  - EXPOSE
  - CMD
- Building a Docker Image
- Running a Docker Container
- Port Mapping
- Testing the application using `curl`
- Basic Docker troubleshooting

## 🛠 Hands-on Practice

- Created a simple Node.js web server.
- Created a Dockerfile.
- Built a Docker image.
- Ran the application inside a Docker container.
- Tested the application on port 3000.
- Learned common Docker errors and their solutions.

## Key Commands

```bash
node app.js
docker build -t day34-node-app:v1 .
docker images
docker run -d -p 3000:3000 --name day34-container day34-node-app:v1
docker ps
curl http://localhost:3000